      "question_id": "Q1",
      "question": "What system or tool is currently used to check room availability and record the reservation — for example, a calendar application, a dedicated room booking portal, or a manual spreadsheet?",
      "answer": "The process uses a calendar system combined with a dedicated room reservation system. These two systems work together to check availability and record the reservation. The specific product names are not specified."
    },
    {
      "question_id": "Q2",
      "question": "What specific inputs must be provided before a reservation can be made — such as meeting date, start and end time, expected number of attendees, or required equipment?",
      "answer": "The required inputs are meeting date and time, participant count, location preference, and equipment needs. These must be collected before availability is checked and a room is selected."
    },
    {
      "question_id": "Q3",
      "question": "When multiple rooms are available for the requested time slot, what criteria determine which room is selected?",
      "answer": "Room selection is based on capacity matching the participant count, required equipment availability, and location preference. If special equipment is needed, that filters the options further; otherwise a standard room is considered sufficient."
    },
    {
      "question_id": "Q4",
      "question": "What happens when no suitable room is available for the requested time — is the meeting rescheduled, moved to an alternative location, or escalated to someone for resolution?",
      "answer": "Room unavailability is listed as an exception in the process. The specific resolution path — rescheduling, alternative location, or escalation — is not specified in the workflow."
    },
    {
      "question_id": "Q5",
      "question": "How is the confirmed room information communicated to participants — for example, through a calendar invite update, an email notification, or a message in a team chat tool?",
      "answer": "After the room is reserved, the organizer creates or updates a calendar invitation and then notifies participants of the room information. An email or collaboration tool is used for notification, though the specific tool is not named."
    },
    {
      "question_id": "Q6",
      "question": "Approximately how many room reservations are made per day or per week, and is there a predictable peak period when demand is highest?",
      "answer": "The volume of reservations per day or week and any peak demand periods are not specified in the workflow."
    }
  ]
}
Task: Incorporate the answers and produce an updated structured workflow representation plus automation opportunities.
Record unknown facts as remaining gaps, rather than asserting unsupported details.
